BullMQ Lua scripts (expanded)
================================

Files in this directory:

  addStandardJob.lua
  moveStalledJobsToWait.lua
  moveToActive.lua
  moveToDelayed.lua
  moveToFinished.lua
  extendLock.lua

Origin
------

Extracted from the locked dependency in this repository:

  node_modules/.pnpm/bullmq@5.63.2/node_modules/bullmq/dist/cjs/scripts/*.js

Each file there embeds the fully expanded script (the `--- @include` directives of
`dist/cjs/commands/*.lua` resolved) as the `content` template literal. The files
here are that embedded content copied verbatim, so the requires/includes and the
function ordering are exactly what BullMQ 5.63.2 executes against Redis.

Mapping from BullMQ command names (and script versions) to file names:

  addStandardJob:9          -> addStandardJob.lua
  moveStalledJobsToWait:8   -> moveStalledJobsToWait.lua
  moveToActive:11           -> moveToActive.lua
  moveToDelayed:8           -> moveToDelayed.lua
  moveToFinished:14         -> moveToFinished.lua
  extendLock:2              -> extendLock.lua

Why the scripts are vendored
----------------------------

api-go and NestJS share the `classification_quality` queue, so a job moved by Go
must be indistinguishable from a job moved by BullMQ. Re-implementing the state
machine in Go would drift; running the same Lua keeps the hash fields, the
wait/active/delayed structures, the lock and the stalled set byte-compatible in
both directions. Only the subset needed by this queue is vendored (no delayed
add, no priorities, no repeat jobs, no parent/child jobs, no rate limiter).

